  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Certain URI's within Fedora 3 FOXML objects contain urls that have values like \"",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "href": "http://local.fedora.server/"
         },
         "type": "link"
        }
       ],
       "text": "http://local.fedora.server/",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "text": "\".  Migrating these into fedora 4 will require special handling.  ",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "For this ticket:",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "1.  Those ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "href": "http://local.fedora.server/something"
         },
         "type": "link"
        }
       ],
       "text": "http://local.fedora.server/something",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "text": "\" urls that would resolve to a resource in fedora 3 that is being migrated to fedora 4 should be migrated such that they resolve to the migrated resource in fedora 4.   There are several URL patterns that resolve to resources \"/fedora/objects/pid/...\", \"/fedora/objects/pid/datastreams/dsid/content\" \"/fedora/get/pid\" \"/fedora/get/pid/datastream/, etc.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "1.  Any \"",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "href": "http://local.fedora.server/"
         },
         "type": "link"
        }
       ],
       "text": "http://local.fedora.server/",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "text": "\" urls that resolve to something other than a fedora resource should result in an exception logged.  I can't imagine why anyone would do such a thing in fedora 3... though we have an example of one in our example foxml for migration-utils.  ",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "href": "https://github.com/fcrepo3/fcrepo/blob/f10f6c1587fb0e074eca90c11bb9b9a4b3d88d89/fcrepo-server/src/main/java/org/fcrepo/server/storage/translation/DOTranslationUtility.java#L91-L93"
         },
         "type": "link"
        }
       ],
       "text": "https://github.com/fcrepo3/fcrepo/blob/f10f6c1587fb0e074eca90c11bb9b9a4b3d88d89/fcrepo-server/src/main/java/org/fcrepo/server/storage/translation/DOTranslationUtility.java#L91-L93",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
